{"e":{"Wemfall":[{"p":"noun","g":"m","i":"/ˈveːmfal/","a":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/40/De-Wemfall.ogg/De-Wemfall.ogg.mp3","s":[["synonym of Dativ: dative case",[],[]]],"fm":[["Wemfalles","genitive"],["Wemfalls","genitive"],["Wemfälle","plural"],["Wemfall","nominative singular"],["Wemfälle","definite nominative plural"],["Wemfalles","genitive singular"],["Wemfalls","genitive singular"],["Wemfälle","definite genitive plural"],["Wemfall","dative singular"],["Wemfalle","dative singular"],["Wemfällen","dative definite plural"],["Wemfall","accusative singular"],["Wemfälle","accusative definite plural"],["Wem-Fall","alternative"]],"et":"wem (“whom”) + Fall (“case”)"}],"Wembley-Tor":[{"p":"noun","g":"n","i":"/ˈwɛmbliˌtoːɐ̯/","a":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/De-Wembley-Tor.ogg/De-Wembley-Tor.ogg.mp3","s":[["A ghost goal; an apparent goal in which it is not clear whether or not the ball crossed the line.",[],[["Mit technischen Raffinessen sollen falsche Abseitspfiffe und „Wembley-Tore\" aus dem Fußball eliminiert werden.","With technical refinements, false offside calls and ghost goals should be eliminated from football."],["Die Franzosen hatten zwei Pfostenschüsse, in der zweiten Halbzeit fast ein Wembley-Tor—was ja, wie jeder weiß, keins war—, es hätte schnell 2:0 oder 3:0 für die Rotweinnation stehen können.","The French had two shots against the post, and in the second half almost a ghost goal—which yes, as everyone knows, was not one—it could have quickly been 2-0 or 3-0 for the red wine nation."]]]],"fm":[["Wembley-Tores","genitive"],["Wembley-Tors","genitive"],["Wembley-Tore","plural"],["Wembley-Tor","nominative singular"],["Wembley-Tore","definite nominative plural"],["Wembley-Tores","genitive singular"],["Wembley-Tors","genitive singular"],["Wembley-Tore","definite genitive plural"],["Wembley-Tor","dative singular"],["Wembley-Tore","dative singular"],["Wembley-Toren","dative definite plural"],["Wem